From 69f1eadc0427bcdf1ccf076e837a8dc874573690 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:00:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] hub admission: pickup's judge binds the owner secret
 scope in the gateway dispatcher; log each unavailable branch

Hub pickup skipped every cache-miss hub-bound foreign card as "hub admission unavailable; retried next
tick" (t_01a1cff283f89392). Reproduced in the live hub gateway (sys.remote_exec probe, fresh-Context
thread like the dispatcher): admit() returned the default Verdict in 0.01 s because call_llm's credential
pool seeding read ANTHROPIC_TOKEN through get_secret with no secret scope bound, and the multiplexing
gateway raises UnscopedSecretError there. The dispatcher ticks in an empty Context; the auto-decomposer
already binds the launch profile's scope, the pickup judge did not. A cache hit reads no credential,
which is why only pre-warmed verdicts got through.

admit() now binds owner_secret_scope(get_hermes_home()) around the judge call when multiplexing is on
and no scope is bound (a creating turn's scope is kept; the judge thread inherits it via copy_context).
Each unavailable branch (routing off, timeout, route mismatch, exception type) and pickup's
in-transaction deferral log a warning naming it.

Tests: tests/test_kanban_hub_admission_dispatcher_scope.py (RED on main: the empty-Context multiplexing
call denies unavailable and nothing is logged; GREEN here).
